{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/EF Core Fluent API.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/EF Core Fluent API.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"ef core fluent api ef core fluent api","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/EF Core Fluent API.md","fileName":"EF Core Fluent API.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"EF Core Fluent API","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-08 21:16\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Entity Framework Core Data Access]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Entity Framework Core Data Access","c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/EF Core Fluent API.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/EF Core Fluent API.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"ef core fluent api ef core fluent api","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/EF Core Fluent API.md","fileName":"EF Core Fluent API.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"EF Core Fluent API","heading":"EF Core Fluent API","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The EF Core Fluent API configures a model through chained method calls, commonly in `OnModelCreating`. It can define keys, property constraints, relationships, indexes, table mappings, value generation, and behavior that conventions do not capture.\n\nFluent configuration keeps persistence details out of entity classes and can express mappings unavailable through attributes. When conventions, annotations, and Fluent API configuration conflict, the explicit Fluent configuration has the greatest authority.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Entity Framework Core Data Access","c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/EF Core Fluent API.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/EF Core Fluent API.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__",